        "agent_output": "## Summary\n\nI found and fixed the bug in `/private/var/folders/46/f_t_23kj4ts9glvnmcb6gr7m0000gn/T/stylebench_m808dkln/src/validators/between.py`.\n\n**The Bug:**\nLines 65-66 had an incorrect early return:\n```python\nif min_val is None:\n    return False\n```\n\nThis caused the function to always return `False` when `min_val` was `None`, which broke the case where only `max_val` was provided (like `between(12, min_val=None, max_val=14)`).\n\n**The Fix:**\nRemoved the incorrect early return. The function now properly handles `None` values by replacing them with `AbsMax()` or `AbsMin()` objects that work with the comparison logic, allowing the function to work correctly when only one boundary is specified.\n\nAll 57 tests now pass, including the previously failing test `test_returns_true_on_valid_range[12-None-14]`.\n",
